Specifications
--------------
The parser and extractors are written from public specifications only:
  - ORCID Message Schema v3.0 (https://github.com/ORCID/orcid-model)
  - ORCID iD structure and check digit, ISO/IEC 7064:2003 MOD 11-2
    (https://support.orcid.org/hc/en-us/articles/360006897674)
  - XML 1.0 (Fifth Edition), W3C Recommendation
  - RFC 8259, The JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) Data Interchange Format,
    and RFC 3629, UTF-8 (the JSON parser, writer and escaping)
  - FIPS 180-4, Secure Hash Standard (SHA-256)
  - POSIX.1-2001 ustar / pax interchange format and the GNU tar long-name
    extension (for reading .tar / .tar.gz dumps)
No code or test data was copied from other ORCID, XML or JSON software.

Third-party material in this repository
---------------------------------------
reference/orcid-model/
  The ORCID message schema v3.0 (XSDs, README and samples for record_3.0,
  common_3.0, summary_3.0, notification_3.0 and group-id-3.0), copied
  unmodified from https://github.com/ORCID/orcid-model at commit
  9592e2d3bde21a1edf703f26f8bc304448f886fb.
  Copyright © 2012-2018 ORCID, Inc. ORCID MIT-style license:
  reference/orcid-model/LICENSE. Provenance: reference/orcid-model/PROVENANCE.md.

reference/orcid-dumps/index.csv
  File listing (names, sizes, MD5s, URLs) of the ORCID Public Data File
  releases as published by ORCID on figshare (https://orcid.figshare.com/).
  The data files themselves are released by ORCID under CC0 1.0.

Test data
---------
test/data/0000-0003-0100-6634.xml is the public ORCID record of
0000-0003-0100-6634 as returned by https://pub.orcid.org/v3.0/. ORCID makes
public record data available under CC0 1.0
(https://info.orcid.org/documentation/integration-guide/orcid-public-data-file/).

test/data/demo/0000-0002-2771-9344.xml is the public ORCID record of
0000-0002-2771-9344 (a fictitious person's record that ORCID uses as an
example), as returned by https://pub.orcid.org/v3.0/0000-0002-2771-9344/record,
unmodified (byte-identical to yorc-rs's tests/data/0000-0002-2771-9344.xml);
CC0 1.0 like the record above. The walkthrough, the recipes and the task
bundles' worked example read it.

Files under test/data/activities/ are single activity items (for example one
full work) taken unmodified from the ORCID Public Data File activities archive,
which ORCID releases under CC0 1.0.

test/data/changes/old.xml is the ORCID sample record
reference/orcid-model/record_3.0/samples/read_samples/record-3.0.xml (fictitious
iD 8888-8888-8888-8880); new.xml is an edited copy of it, made for the
orcid_changes tests.

test/data/dump/ holds two small archives in the layout of the ORCID Public Data
File, built for the tests from the two records above plus synthetic members
(long names, non-XML files).

Files under test/data/errors/ are the summaries of a locked and a deprecated
record (error documents) taken unmodified from the ORCID Public Data File 2025
summaries archive, which ORCID releases under CC0 1.0.

test/data/json/orcid_test_json.tar is a tar archive, built for the tests,
of two ORCID schema samples (reference/orcid-model, ORCID MIT-style license)
and a one-line text file.

test/data/synthetic/coauthors-bulk.xml was written by hand for this repository
(two invented works in a bulk response, to the ORCID work and bulk XSDs) and is
covered by its MIT license.

test/data/releases/ holds two synthetic Public Data File "releases" built by
scripts/make_release_fixtures.py from six summaries of the ORCID Public Data
File 2025 (CC0 1.0): the 2024 archive has five of them unchanged, the 2025
archive applies the edits listed in that script.
